{"version":"scxml.report/v3","kind":"validator","validator":{"source_name":"tests/ui/limit008-done-state-over-name-bound.scx","source_text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" initial=\"\">\n  <state id=\"\">\n    <final id=\"done\"/>\n  </state>\n</scxml>\n","diagnostics":[{"severity":"error","code":"LIMIT008","category":"semantic","message":"state ID `sxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx…` is 1,014 bytes, so the `done.state.` event it raises is 1,025 bytes, more than the 1,024 an event name may have","primary":{"span":{"start":1100,"end":2114},"message":"`done.state.` and these 1,014 bytes make 1,025"},"secondary":[],"notes":["SCXML 1.0 §3.7: on entering a `<final>` child the processor \"MUST generate the event done.state.id\" where id is the parent state's ID (a `<parallel>` raises it when a `<final>` is entered in one of its `<state>` regions and every other region is in a final state, §3.7 and Appendix D); every build bounds an event name to 1,024 bytes of UTF-8, so this state could never complete; SCXML 1.0 sets no length, and this is the implementation's bound (spec errata L.6)"],"help":"shorten the ID to at most 1,013 bytes and update every reference to it","spec_references":["SCXML 1.0 §3.7 <final>"],"fixes":[]}],"counts":{"errors":1,"warnings":0,"notes":0,"total":1}}}